# Use-case 02 gap 5 (claim C1) -- FIXED 2026-08-26 by the
# template-clone isolation change (ADR-005): a `_` hole belongs to its
# NEAREST ENCLOSING GENERATOR, so close() around a pack whose template
# holds a hole no longer reports that hole as its own. The overlay
# statement now merges with the generated child exactly as it does
# without close(): dev {x:1}, prod {x:2}. Historically the outer
# close() call saw the template's hole (hasPlace crossed the generator
# boundary), so the overlay was absorbed INTO the template -- every
# child grew a bogus `prod:` map, prod.x stayed 1, exit 0.
# Pinned in both engines: test/spec/gen-close.tsv
# close-pack-hole-overlay-merges.
# expected: {"d":...,"deploy":{"dev":{"x":1},"prod":{"x":2}}} exit 0
# actual:   {"d":...,"deploy":{"dev":{"x":1},"prod":{"x":2}}} exit 0
d: { dev: {}, prod: {} }
deploy: close(pack($.d, _ & { x: ***1 | integer }))
deploy: prod: x: 2
